Description: session broker for the fastrdp multi-user RDP terminal server
 fastrdp turns a Linux host into a multi-user RDP terminal server:
 freerdp-proxy3 is the single front end, a session broker decides which
 back end (xrdp, GNOME Remote Desktop, KRdp) a user gets, and one-time
 tokens let the back ends accept only broker-approved logins.
 .
 This package contains fastrdp-brokerd (Python, standard library only),
 the fastrdpctl admin command, the systemd unit, the PAM service used for
 password and account checks, and a default /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml (realm
 and SSSD domains from the host's krb5.conf and sssd.conf). It also has
 the TERMSRV keytab helpers: fastrdp-termsrv-check (AES keys for NLA) and
 fastrdp-termsrv-keytab with a path unit that copies the TERMSRV keys for
 the proxy whenever Active Directory rotates the machine password, the host
 check fastrdp-check-host and fastrdp-defaults, which installs the default
 configuration of the fastrdp packages and keeps local changes on upgrades.
 .
 The services are installed disabled; check /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml,
 then enable fastrdp-brokerd.service (and on AD hosts
 fastrdp-termsrv-keytab.path). Install fastrdp-server for the whole server.

